{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-ba636dfcf47a79de","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/_dev/GLB/stepwise-fifa-qa/workflow/instances/quality-engineering-planning/sessions/Test-Strategy-1/refinements/test-master-plan/1787326773416-7fvedfar/sandbox/artifacts/outputs/quality-engineering-planning/MTP-SPEC-Test-Strategy-1.md\" lines=\"340\" start=\"1\" end=\"340\" returned=\"340\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|---\n     2|version: 1.0.0\n     3|project: InsideFIFA-WEB\n     4|generated_at: 2025-01-21T20:48:28Z\n     5|session_id: Test-Strategy-1\n     6|---\n     7|\n     8|## scope_matrix\n     9|| epic_id | title | priority_tier | test_priority | mapped_frs | dependencies | complexity |\n    10||---------|-------|---------------|---------------|------------|--------------|------------|\n    11|| EPIC-001 | Core Navigation Test Framework | Must Have | P0 | [FR-001, FR-005] | None | High |\n    12|| EPIC-002 | Homepage Functionality and Navigation Validation | Must Have | P0 | [FR-001] | EPIC-001 | Medium |\n    13|| EPIC-003 | \"What FIFA Does\" Subpages Navigation Testing | Must Have | P0 | [FR-002] | EPIC-001, EPIC-002 | Medium |\n    14|| EPIC-004 | Top Navigation \"Inside FIFA\" Menu Validation | Must Have | P0 | [FR-003] | EPIC-001 | Medium |\n    15|| EPIC-005 | Multi-language Testing Capability | Should Have | P1 | [FR-004] | EPIC-001, EPIC-002, EPIC-003, EPIC-004 | High |\n    16|| EPIC-006 | Cross-browser Testing Extension | Could Have | P2 | [FR-005] | EPIC-001 | High |\n    17|| EPIC-007 | Multi-viewport Testing Support | Could Have | P2 | [FR-005] | EPIC-006 | Medium |\n    18|\n    19|### in_scope_features\n    20|- Core navigation framework setup and validation\n    21|- Homepage functionality testing\n    22|- \"What FIFA Does\" content areas navigation (7 topic pages)\n    23|- Top navigation \"Inside FIFA\" menu testing\n    24|- Multi-language framework support (English, Spanish, French)\n    25|- Cross-browser expansion capability\n    26|- Responsive design testing for multiple viewports\n    27|\n    28|### out_of_scope_features\n    29|- Authentication-based page testing\n    30|- Database validation\n    31|- API endpoint testing\n    32|- Server-side performance testing\n    33|- Security penetration testing\n    34|- Content management system testing\n    35|- Third-party integration testing\n    36|\n    37|### scope_verification\n    38|total_epics: 7\n    39|in_scope_count: 7\n    40|out_of_scope_count: 0\n    41|coverage_percentage: 100%\n    42|\n    43|## risk_assessment\n    44|| risk_id | description | source | impact | likelihood | test_mitigation | priority |\n    45||---------|-------------|--------|--------|------------|----------------|----------|\n    46|| QR-001 | Website structure changes breaking navigation tests | RSK-001 | High | Medium | Implement robust selectors and regular test maintenance | P0 |\n    47|| QR-002 | Rate limiting or IP blocking during automated access | RSK-002 | Medium | Medium | Implement test delays and consider rotating IP addresses | P1 |\n    48|| QR-003 | Content localization variations across languages | RSK-003 | Medium | Medium | Create language-specific test configurations | P1 |\n    49|| QR-004 | Browser compatibility issues affecting test reliability | RSK-004 | Low | Low | Version-specific test configurations and regular updates | P2 |\n    50|| QR-005 | Page load times exceeding 3-second target | NFR-001 | High | Low | Performance monitoring and load time validation | P0 |\n    51|| QR-006 | Test pass rate below 95% reliability target | NFR-002 | High | Low | Comprehensive test coverage and stable test environment | P0 |\n    52|| QR-007 | Test suite updates taking longer than 2 hours for UI changes | NFR-003 | Medium | Medium | Modular test design and page object model | P1 |\n    53|| QR-008 | Cross-platform compatibility failures on desktop viewport | NFR-004 | Medium | Low | Viewport-specific test configurations | P1 |\n    54|\n    55|### risk_priority_matrix\n    56|| priority | risk_count | risks |\n    57||----------|------------|-------|\n    58|| P0 | 3 | QR-001, QR-005, QR-006 |\n    59|| P1 | 3 | QR-002, QR-003, QR-007 |\n    60|| P2 | 2 | QR-004, QR-008 |\n    61|\n    62|### risk_response_strategy\n    63|- **P0 Risks:** Immediate mitigation required, blocking issues\n    64|- **P1 Risks:** Mitigation planned, monitored closely\n    65|- **P2 Risks:** Accepted with monitoring, contingency plans available\n    66|\n    67|## test_strategy\n    68|### test_levels\n    69|| level | description | scope | automation_percentage |\n    70||-------|-------------|-------|----------------------|\n    71|| unit | Component-level testing of page objects and utilities | Individual functions and methods | 90% |\n    72|| integration | API and service integration testing | Browser automation framework | 80% |\n    73|| system_e2e | End-to-end user journey testing | Full navigation flows | 95% |\n    74|| performance | Load time and response validation | Page load metrics | 70% |\n    75|| security | Basic security validation | Input validation and XSS | 30% |\n    76|| accessibility | WCAG compliance testing | Screen reader and keyboard navigation | 40% |\n    77|\n    78|### test_types_by_priority\n    79|| priority | test_types | execution_frequency |\n    80||----------|------------|-------------------|\n    81|| P0 | Smoke tests, critical path navigation, performance validation | Every commit |\n    82|| P1 | Functional regression, multi-language validation, cross-browser basic | Daily |\n    83|| P2 | Cross-browser full coverage, responsive design, visual regression | Weekly |\n    84|\n    85|### nfr_test_approaches\n    86|| nfr_id | test_approach | measurement_criteria | tools |\n    87||--------|---------------|---------------------|-------|\n    88|| NFR-001 | Page load time monitoring | Average < 3 seconds across 5 runs | Browser performance API |\n    89|